WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.860
Trace the physical power path without skipping connections.

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.660
Begin at the defined facility input, follow conversion in the shelf, then

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.540
distribution and equipment power entry.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.000
For each segment, identify its current, voltage, thermal and fault requirements using

5
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.260
the selected implementation.

6
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.560
Connections can become limiting even when the surrounding conductors appear adequate.

7
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.920
Their applicable rating depends on the assembly and operating conditions, not just

8
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:25.980
a connector family name.

9
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.160
Likewise, a busbar drawing describes a defined interface; it doesn't validate every

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.280
attachment or equipment population around it.

11
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.900
Keep the protective bonding path distinct from the operating return.

12
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.680
The source grounding scheme controls those functions.

13
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.780
Don't reinterpret a simplified course schematic as installation guidance.

14
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.800
The review outcome is a traceable path in which no segment relies

15
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.260
on an unrelated rating or an assumed bond.

16
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.400
If the power shelf changes revision, revisit the affected input, output, management

17
00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.060
and mechanical boundaries instead of assuming the old integration evidence transfers unchanged.

